course: dictionary
lesson: 9375
title: Sport and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sport is a game or activity where you move your body and follow rules, often to win. Football, swimming and netball are all sports. Sport can also mean all these activities together, and in the UK we say sport, while in the USA they say sports.
explain: Context helps you see which meaning is right. In «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.», sport means the activity itself. In «Maddox's mum can't come to sports day», sports day is a day of games and races at school.
explain: Some words change their meaning with the words next to them. A good sport is someone who plays fairly and is kind whether they win or lose. «Saying sorry to the other team's player helps put it right» shows what a good sport does. To sport something means to wear it proudly, to show it off.
fact: A sport is a game or activity with rules, where you move your body.
fact: Sport (UK) and sports (USA) both mean all these activities together.
fact: «A good sport» means someone who plays fairly and is kind, win or lose.
fact: «Sport» can also be a verb: to sport something means to wear it to show it off.
fact: Phrases to know: play sport, team sport, sports day, sports centre, water sports.
exercise: In «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.», what does sport mean? | A rule book | A type of breakfast food | A place where people sit and watch | *Activities like football or swimming, where you move your body and follow rules
exercise: Ravi says sorry to the other team after a foul. What does that make him? | *A good sport | A sports centre | A team sport | A water sport
exercise: «Good sports clubs, like boxing or judo clubs, have strict rules against fighting outside the club.» Find and copy one word that means very firm and must be obeyed. | outside | *strict | boxing | fighting
test: «In Leeds, Maddox's mum can't come to sports day.» What is a sports day? | *A day of races and games at school | A day for cooking porridge | A day when the shops are closed | A day off for the holidays
test: Which sentence uses sport to mean wearing something to show it off? | Sport is good for your health. | *She likes to sport her new bright trainers at school. | The sports centre opens at nine. | They play sport every Tuesday after school.
exam: Choose the best word: Porridge and fruit give steady energy before ___. | *sport | sported | sporting | sporty
